{
  "#": "Scrub manifest for the storage collector: the union of every payload its pools collection captures \u2014 zpool status -j (status.json), zpool list -j -p -v (list.json) and the device alias map (devlinks.json). Same tree of pools and vdevs in the first two, at different depths: status nests root -> raidz -> disks, list starts at the raidz, so the vdev entries repeat per depth for the union of members each depth carries. devlinks shares no root with either, which is what the payload-scoped entries at the bottom are for.",
  "#names": "Pool and vdev dicts are keyed by the very names their rows repeat, so every such level carries a '~key' entry. The keys mix classes the pattern language cannot split \u2014 a pool name somebody chose, zpool's own structural names (raidz1-0), and by-id WWNs \u2014 so they take the free-text pass (format name): the WWN spelling is substituted, the structural names carry nothing it matches, and the pool name is handed to the run as --hostnames, which is the one global-substring mechanism the tool has for operator-chosen words.",
  "#identity": "guid is the identifier that survives rename and import \u2014 identity at every depth, guid_u64 because zpool status emits it as a JSON integer and zpool list as a digit string; one entry serves both spellings and derives the same replacement, which is the cross-file join the specimen teaches. devid spells the WWN as scsi-3<16hex> (no 0x \u2014 the spelling the old scrubber missed) and path embeds it as by-id; both identity.",
  "#phys_path": "A bus address locates a card on a bus and is identical across every machine of that model \u2014 the field the shape-guessing scrubber rewrote into the documentation range (DESIGN 21). The manifest, not shape, is what says it stays.",
  "#nothing": "States, error counters, sizes, scan statistics, txg, feature versions and property tables are measurements and verdicts \u2014 the same on every machine that has them.",
